WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.934
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.467
We hope you're doing well.
And now, if you don't mind,

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.801
we're going to get to the news.
President Biden visited

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:10.501
an Amtrak maintenance facility
today in Delaware.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.834
So we got an extra hour
of sleep this weekend,

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.801
but he sure didn't.
"I'm too excited."

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.200
Former President Trump
took the witness stand today

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.934
in his civil fraud trial.
He swore to tell the truth,

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.834
the whole truth and nothing
but the truth,

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.501
and then everyone
just laughed and laughed.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:33.033
While testifying during his
civil fraud trial today,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.300
former President Trump said

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.968
that he believes
his Mar a Lago resort

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.334
is worth between
$1 billion and $1.5 billion.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.667
Oh. Very smart.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.567
The insanity defense.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:48.000
Dude, you bought it
for $10,000,000 in 1985,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.901
and now it's worth 1.5 billion?

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:55.501
The only way I would believe
that is if it was in Brooklyn.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:59.033
Then that's about right.
Maybe a little low.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.334
While testifying today,

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.167
former President Trump
also appeared to forget

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.501
that he wasn't president
in 2021.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:08.868
Well, so did half the country.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.100
After FBI agents raided the home

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.033
of his chief fundraiser
last week,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.868
New York Mayor Eric Adams said,
quote,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.334
"Where there's smoke,
there's not always fire."

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:23.334
Ah, yes,
that famous expression.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.300
Okay, so we found out
he's shady.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.868
But you know what they say --
late is worse than never.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.934
The third Republican
presidential primary debate

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:38.534
will be held Wednesday in Miami
or, as it's now dubbed,

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:42.634
"Who Wants to Be
a Vice President?"

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.367
Pennsylvania Senator
John Fetterman

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.901
criticized California Governor
Gavin Newsom over the weekend

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.834
and said he was secretly
running for president,

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.200
as opposed to Fetterman,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.400
who looks like
he's running for

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.367
guy who doesn't wipe down
the equipment at the gym.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:02:00.767
Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg
revealed on Friday

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.701
that he tore his ACL
while training

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.567
for a competitive MMA fight.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.434
Apparently,
what happened was

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.033
there was a coffee table
in the way.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.133
The fastest runner in
the New York City Marathon

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.434
yesterday
finished the course

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.300
in just under two hours
and five minutes,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:26.200
a full ten minutes faster
than if he had taken the bus.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.801
Better luck next year, the bus.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.167
Archeologists in Germany believe
they've discovered

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.801
the ancient remains
of a husband and wife

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:37.801
buried in the same casket.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.200
Her idea.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.267
Baz!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.701
We're going to win them back
with this one.

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:54.934
And finally, the American
Ornithological -- Ornith--

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.734
Oh, Jesus.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.501
I said this word wrong
last week,

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:01.667
and I got a lot of angry notes
from ornithologists.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:05.501
And now I'm in my head about it.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.968
And finally, the American
Bird People Society

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.667
announced --
It's fine.

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:15.501
It's an either/or.
It's famously an either/or.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:18.234
Announced last week that it
is renaming birds

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.801
that are currently named
after problematic people,

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.901
though in retrospect,
it was never really fair

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:23.901
to name that one

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.200
Jared from Subway.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.968
And... that was a monologue,
everybody.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:29.968
We're up and running.

